<article class="env-lemma" id="00SW">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/00SW">Lemma <span data-tag="00SW">10.136.13</span>.</a> A relative global complete intersection is syntomic, i.e., flat. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $R \to S$ be a relative global complete intersection. The fibres are global complete intersections, and $S$ is of finite presentation over $R$. Thus the only thing to prove is that $R \to S$ is flat. This is true by (2) of Lemma <a href="/tag/00SV" data-tag="00SV">10.136.12</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>